Calc: outside Windows an asked update names every DDE source

0086 names a DDE source when its update fails. Outside Windows svl's
DDE is a stub (svl/unx/source/svdde/ddedummy.cxx): every connection
reports no error and carries no data, so a link to a server that is
not there updated as if it were read. No DDE server can answer there,
so the update leaves the link alone and names it as not read.

diff --git a/sc/source/ui/docshell/docsh4.cxx b/sc/source/ui/docshell/docsh4.cxx
--- a/sc/source/ui/docshell/docsh4.cxx
+++ b/sc/source/ui/docshell/docsh4.cxx
@@ -325,10 +325,15 @@
         }
         else if (auto pDde = dynamic_cast<ScDdeLink*>(xLink.get()))
         {
+#ifdef _WIN32
             if (pDde->Update())
                 bDde = true;
             else
                 rFailed.push_back(pDde->GetAppl() + "|" + pDde->GetTopic());
+#else
+            // DDE is Windows only; elsewhere it never reads.
+            rFailed.push_back(pDde->GetAppl() + "|" + pDde->GetTopic());
+#endif
         }
